# RFC-GPACK-001 §26/§27 — valid-corpus fixture: a consumer pack with TWO
# semantic dependencies.
#
# §26: dependencies are pack-owned semantic declarations; a dependency MUST
# declare which surfaces are required; Scope is a subset of
# {SEMANTICS, LAW, PROJECTION}. Each gp:PackRequirement below carries
# gp:dependencyScope EXACTLY {SEMANTICS} — one scope token, no LAW, no
# PROJECTION. The token form is witnessed by the RFC's own receipt envelope
# (§55: "scope": ["SEMANTICS"]); scope individuals (IRI form) are spec-pack
# vocabulary territory (T01) and deliberately not invented here.
#
# §27: a semantic dependency imports admitted graph semantics WITHOUT
# activating projection: ImportSemantics(Q) does NOT imply RunProjection(Q).
#
# §73: the dependee packs (deps/alpha-semantics-pack, deps/beta-semantics-pack)
# are semantic-only — no templates/ directory. A Core pack MAY contain no
# projections. Engines whose implementation requires at least one template
# MUST report semantic-only execution as UNSUPPORTED rather than redefine
# the abstract Pack to require projection.
#
# Resolution note for wave-2 courts: the dependee pack sources live inline
# under deps/ beside this pack; a court resolves the gp:requiresPack IRIs by
# registering those directories explicitly.

@prefix gp: <https://ggen.dev/ns/pack#> .

<urn:ggen:pack:two-semantic-dependencies>
    a gp:Pack ;
    gp:name "two-semantic-dependencies" ;
    gp:version "1.0.0" ;
    gp:profile gp:Portable1 ;
    gp:authorityCeiling gp:Construct .

<urn:ggen:pack:two-semantic-dependencies#requirement-alpha>
    a gp:PackRequirement ;
    gp:requiresPack <urn:ggen:pack:alpha-semantics-pack> ;
    gp:dependencyScope "SEMANTICS" .

<urn:ggen:pack:two-semantic-dependencies#requirement-beta>
    a gp:PackRequirement ;
    gp:requiresPack <urn:ggen:pack:beta-semantics-pack> ;
    gp:dependencyScope "SEMANTICS" .
